header.assumptions:
Short-end wrap candidate screen. No adopted baseline files are modified.
Conservative retained legacy hydraulic head plus explicit NEW short-end friction/minors;
no speculative mass or pressure credit for removed legacy routes. Folded wraps rigid.

settled_optics.scope:
Differential Nusselt contour screen on settled final Newton rigid geometry.
Same inherited three radiator points/panel. This tests the no-optical-credit decision;
not a new array-temperature/reradiation, bus-occlusion or flexible-body qualification.

yoke_loads.scope:
Conservative repaired-yoke load transfer from final rigid deployment.
Root-moment plus force-times-full-span is an intentionally conservative envelope;
not a substitute for joint fitting/bearing/local distortion qualification.

stages/spin1/THERMAL_SPIN1.json.doc:
SPIN1 thermal rerun (box CPU, scipy brentq; same model as the frozen baseline's operating(): v2: Al6061 26/0.225 Warp fin table (fin_v2.py), area factor 1.0 (was F3_L40_t0p5 / K13D 0.9913), 0.44 K MC margin,
pmad 0.92, aux 2 kW, rack rise 20 K at the load, radiator rise = 20 K x Q/IT). Knobs added (defaults reproduce the frozen baseline exactly):
  fluid: 'water_proxy' (rho 978, cp 4180, mu 4e-4 = baseline CT.G) or 'MPG40' (CoolProp INCOMP::MPG[0.4] at the rack-mean temperature, iterated);
         MPG40 hydraulic penalty: rack and column dp scaled by mu_MPG40/mu_model (laminar-conservative, ASSUMED), trunk via Re (CT.cool);
  extra_heat_W: added heat into the main radiator (battery-recharge PMAD loss);  F_scale: emission view multiplier (bumper ridge blockage).
Plate resistance 14.22 K/kW and HBM 18 K/load-fraction are unchanged (inherited).
